#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "836f2f1b-5dd4-5dba-81cc-eb9ffe7db8d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4693" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_2 := R_2 +(- 4) \\cdot R_1$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_2:=R_2 + (-4) R_1$ means that we need to add $-4$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nCarrying out this row operation, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4+(-4)(1) & 2+(-4)(2) & -1+(-4)(3) \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "2ff0a6f5-f3b2-5b39-8b69-1a0c969548cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-4694" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/id #uuid "a24c9621-793b-5c60-9c47-2b452f0faa2b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4695" :question/problem "Which elementary row operation could transform the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has been changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nNow, applying the operation $R_2:=R_2+1 \\cdot R_1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4+1\\cdot (-4) & 1+1\\cdot (-2) & 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation could be done by the operation \n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+1\\cdot R_1\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+R_1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059507 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}] :question/id #uuid "f8417bbc-b748-519b-a997-fbb4aed755eb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4696" :question/problem "Given that\n$[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ which elementary row operation could make $a_{22}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "In the given matrix, we have $a_{22}=5$ and we want to perform an elementary row operation that makes $a_{22}=0.$\n\n- We *cannot* make $a_{22}=0$ by switching two rows, because there are no rows with $0$ as the second entry.\n\n- We *cannot* multiply the second row by $0,$ because we are only allowed to multiply rows by *nonzero* constants.\n\n- However, we *can* add a multiple of another row to the $2$nd row to make $a_{22}=0.$\n\nLooking at the first row, we see that $a_{12}=1.$ If we add $-5$ times this entry to $a_{22},$ we will get $a_{22}=0$ as desired. So, the elementary row operation that we need to use is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1.\n$$\n\nApplying this operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1+(-5)\\cdot 3 & 5+(-5)\\cdot 1 & 6+(-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -16 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the desired elemetary row operation is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1,\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 -5 R_1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92e38ca4-c738-5e47-a590-b209a3d19694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056007} {:answer/id #uuid "eda762ac-ee3e-50f6-b681-57fa7be2c3f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056008} {:answer/id #uuid "093a0c72-f1b7-5143-b70c-d653458bfae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056009} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5a4ff3-d3c6-5e6c-a562-48f391f1c0e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056010} {:answer/id #uuid "7741dff9-2dd2-5fda-9925-b08bab5c6f2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda762ac-ee3e-50f6-b681-57fa7be2c3f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056008} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6e3ea1a-3f7e-5525-8cb4-96b911f3655c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00a500f4-f378-5f41-9cd3-c3d0604af452" :question/math-academy-id "q-10217" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5+(-1)(5) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(-1) & 1+(-1)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e94d933-1292-5d19-9c61-76c6a30da8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303740} {:answer/id #uuid "86844dec-65ec-5d2f-8476-0a0966f37846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303741} {:answer/id #uuid "641c11a3-8590-5e38-bef4-9e11aacadcf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303742} {:answer/id #uuid "879fd200-a145-5245-bc88-78b31af276a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303743} {:answer/id #uuid "d99ac1ea-75ae-554c-9428-8713d7e4a534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d99ac1ea-75ae-554c-9428-8713d7e4a534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303744} :answer-field/id #uuid "011ea227-cd6b-5e60-be27-222ce348a871" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94d28327-3100-5e77-acac-c58bb1afa861" :question/math-academy-id "q-10244" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c446ec29-13e0-55fa-9e32-45e5ff1a7468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303747} {:answer/id #uuid "2be7c1ed-aac3-5540-9b6f-3186ecef5984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303748} {:answer/id #uuid "4a599b53-f226-5344-87c7-cb51bcf132d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303749} {:answer/id #uuid "1a04f7f7-d117-59b2-939f-e5fcf2277ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303750} {:answer/id #uuid "88653b97-b9f1-548a-b8ee-69abdb4b501c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a599b53-f226-5344-87c7-cb51bcf132d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303749} :answer-field/id #uuid "0472c2c6-804e-561e-b6f7-9db0c550e50f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d89fad28-1b46-55f3-b90e-6ed4c3f194da" :question/math-academy-id "q-10245" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $B?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4+(4)(1) & 12+(4)(3) & 3+(4)(6) \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1+1 & 2+3 & 4+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a9bba7-f581-5372-a873-0fc17a55fb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056037} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c177a1-6771-55e3-bd09-bf47def49ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056038} {:answer/id #uuid "0d1d8e7e-44fc-5700-9bdc-f19ade4437e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056039} {:answer/id #uuid "5f95897b-76c9-50f9-ba67-9a60ae42a4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056040} {:answer/id #uuid "64489d72-05e0-5199-9ab5-2517bee16eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64489d72-05e0-5199-9ab5-2517bee16eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056041} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe11ff0e-55ca-57c1-896c-442215af5968" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73199f2e-4821-5c88-b3d1-fc53d8677008" :question/math-academy-id "q-10248" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(2) & 9+(3)(4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8366f60-384e-59a5-b340-77b093773b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056043} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf9cd3c-29a4-5216-8be0-0e76b1d81d46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056044} {:answer/id #uuid "fadca7d6-5f5a-5a4e-a1c9-ebcdb2d7de24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056045} {:answer/id #uuid "00bed096-b559-5778-8c19-a43efa2cd149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056046} {:answer/id #uuid "71c75f4c-d383-5832-958e-2f6938509e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00bed096-b559-5778-8c19-a43efa2cd149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056046} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b887faa-7205-58d0-a47b-3ae6cadf6556" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "855eebc5-e47a-5262-b735-bfa0d3ece889" :question/math-academy-id "q-10250" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79015750-280a-5d95-bc2d-b110e5e31c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -\\frac{8}{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303754} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5379c6-ef0c-5d61-b7ef-f3e5f3d16489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303755} {:answer/id #uuid "2b2f76b1-8986-5c05-982f-5df431b961a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303756} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3443bf-0685-543c-ba75-ea41d82d0cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303757} {:answer/id #uuid "1418b72b-2afd-57c6-ad33-07c3a0805b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b2f76b1-8986-5c05-982f-5df431b961a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303756} :answer-field/id #uuid "122ffef5-c2d8-5dfa-8c63-5f500c860742" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f08a2c2-eb16-5d85-a714-beb36e4a0c94" :question/math-academy-id "q-130071" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:=(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 6 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot (-3) & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 9 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a66fe5d-99c6-50a1-8dd0-2bfdf26188c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303761} {:answer/id #uuid "a680c5fd-f83d-5b29-9e4d-996bb9ba9e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303762} {:answer/id #uuid "feb9bda7-c609-5e9e-94c2-c8e6e44d91f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303763} {:answer/id #uuid "497d59d9-ad3d-5e2b-bfe2-a86e8abe6dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303764} {:answer/id #uuid "bf35f16a-1ebc-5434-a2f0-bf2b3606d964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 9 & -7 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a680c5fd-f83d-5b29-9e4d-996bb9ba9e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303762} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae95e35e-7214-5649-b004-be41d40c67a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37f7576f-ad33-50dc-9b99-0070faaebd2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130072" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4+(-1)(-1) & 4+(-1)(9) & 6+(-1)(-2) & 7+(-1)(6) \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c447dfa5-a9b0-5db1-8e6e-876bad94c896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303768} {:answer/id #uuid "16c897ca-87fe-5d91-97f9-6100801f9421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303769} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4528bb-cb33-53b2-9709-8f35d0caae11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303770} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3fe4fc-6591-5a01-9780-4712432f2e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303771} {:answer/id #uuid "029ae91a-4117-50a8-9c95-82893d0d2163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{10})\\cdot {R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c447dfa5-a9b0-5db1-8e6e-876bad94c896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303768} :answer-field/id #uuid "862d9f74-d4be-5bf3-a22f-ffe0d62845dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3d65526-4014-502b-a3c6-a6538d0c4e88" :question/math-academy-id "q-130087" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $2$nd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6dd7ee0-eff3-5149-9711-e60607c6fbdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303775} {:answer/id #uuid "eba705ca-94d4-52aa-9011-e9c8b85b2315" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=3\\cdot {R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303776} {:answer/id #uuid "682b8f5e-399b-518b-b219-9deba15df7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303777} {:answer/id #uuid "01062b74-e719-5bd9-89b8-9f8977629eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-\\frac{4}{7})\\cdot {R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303778} {:answer/id #uuid "01bf9546-f7c6-50b5-a629-2234b7111b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eba705ca-94d4-52aa-9011-e9c8b85b2315" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=3\\cdot {R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303776} :answer-field/id #uuid "768ecd28-2417-5e7a-b8db-3833bfca3468" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97ec1c2d-b02b-554f-ad6f-316e53fd3897" :question/math-academy-id "q-130095" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix  $C$ into the matrix $D$, where \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=3\\cdot {R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a82c6a-e362-5ace-a989-0eeec2bd6f1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303782} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce5a669-1c80-5025-accc-912f22a0c58e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=(-\\frac{3}{8})\\cdot {R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303783} {:answer/id #uuid "59cbfde2-fbc3-5389-8d76-6e5820b8b784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=(-\\frac{8}{3})\\cdot {R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303784} {:answer/id #uuid "4fde6ee0-9fc6-5e95-94f0-e68a513f4f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303785} {:answer/id #uuid "11acf7bb-dbc8-542e-873a-c88a5f8c6b22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01a82c6a-e362-5ace-a989-0eeec2bd6f1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303782} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae4347f5-9c5d-549b-ac48-61bb96bcc333" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a29313ba-5280-5024-8d89-692c77d56928" :question/math-academy-id "q-130100" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $E$ into the matrix $F$, where\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $2$nd row and the $3$rd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $2$nd and the $3$rd row, we notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "244ba311-6d39-5e7a-873d-7c1e694c8a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303789} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2ed31e-51d8-533f-aeca-5d84abdd1017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303790} {:answer/id #uuid "438b2e59-539c-5152-84a4-5b9d2165c1bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303791} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa3c56f-ec98-564e-bff4-9dcf54797632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303792} {:answer/id #uuid "a524de75-edc9-57fe-9c17-dccb2d520e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "244ba311-6d39-5e7a-873d-7c1e694c8a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303789} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6810500-4627-5b65-9c93-028292400d77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31819a12-f2d2-51e4-a7d4-6a1c6ab3a626" :question/math-academy-id "q-130103" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/ti