$C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{22}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991e3e8a-9fae-5d49-bf20-3e73ad09a651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303831} {:answer/id #uuid "16f1456c-a49f-5292-bff6-d5d68cc61f17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303832} {:answer/id #uuid "b40863de-c6ca-598f-a666-6295cf70cd3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303833} {:answer/id #uuid "bb783518-5b0a-5f87-89ae-18359ba2a2a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303834} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd81525-a1f9-5c2f-bfb7-2a7d18c5ce3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16f1456c-a49f-5292-bff6-d5d68cc61f17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303832} :answer-field/id #uuid "8abf023e-83f5-5c6e-9ccb-926042f5a7d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f1ba7f0-e4f6-511d-875d-abce33676c37" :question/math-academy-id "q-72760" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $X?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & 5+(-1)(3) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(1) \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b03b377e-52c2-5601-836e-0c789017abce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303838} {:answer/id #uuid "c03faa06-1be8-5785-ad4e-1882eb8bd0cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303839} {:answer/id #uuid "67fc3f05-1890-562d-97df-b11ac7651db2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303840} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab77215-1622-5a98-b3bc-f51de2ab2d52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303841} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6fc5fc-3932-5a19-b6f9-ae7bc20821e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c03faa06-1be8-5785-ad4e-1882eb8bd0cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303839} :answer-field/id #uuid "a678e252-cf00-5cad-b213-20ce8b5eb303" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37f94344-aca2-5d87-b57e-e260d336958f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72786" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $U?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1 & -3+0 & 4+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00473e68-2cb8-5b58-a46e-51b025f68b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303845} {:answer/id #uuid "62ab899d-84a0-5af9-974c-72c791d83029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303846} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3fcd95-1c35-5ebc-b1af-ffff86b9129d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303847} {:answer/id #uuid "27378b39-be90-56f8-987b-4e97258dc8d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303848} {:answer/id #uuid "acf3b52f-a355-5cb8-9b00-4f8a3f048118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c3fcd95-1c35-5ebc-b1af-ffff86b9129d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303847} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0f1e43-cd5c-518d-9ae6-04d3598f9151" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81299737-4447-5a48-bbe4-83e6cd93672b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72856" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $K$ into the matrix $L$, where\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,L=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}K & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =L.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.\n$$"}]}
